From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:27:27 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Meridian: the first 1.x window on a 0.x profile explains
 the keychain question

From 0.x (signed by Meridian itself) to 1.x (Apple's Developer ID) macOS
asks about "Meridian Safe Storage" before the first window, and at every
start until Always Allow. The note in Restart to update could never show:
it needed a 0.x app running 1.x's code. Now the first window of 1.x on a
profile last opened by 0.x shows the system-ask sheet for it (macOS only,
once): the keychain window drawn with Always Allow glowing.
- update::FirstStartAfterZeroX (unit-tested); "safe-storage" kind in
  system_ask / mac_ask, with no System Settings button.
- The dead note in the update sheet is gone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
